{# The way into a « Visionnage »'s player, from wherever the travail is read - the dashboard card,
   the « Derniers travaux » column and the travail's own page all include this rather than building
   their own href, so a single screen carries the viewing and a single rule decides whether there is
   anything to view.

   `rewatch` only changes the wording. A watching stays open once it is done: the video is the
   course, and a student revising it is doing exactly what it was given for - « Visionner » there
   would suggest it is still owed.

   Nothing is drawn when the travail carries no video: a « Visionnage » saved without one - which
   the Paramétrage form still allows - would otherwise offer a button onto a screen that does not
   exist (App\Controller\StudentWorkController::video answers 404). #}
{% if assignment.videoResource %}
    <a href="{{ path('app_student_work_video', {assignmentId: assignment.id}) }}"
       class="{{ link_class|default('cm-tw-link') }}">
        {{ (rewatch|default(false) ? 'studentWorkRewatchAction' : 'studentWorkWatchAction')|trans }}
    </a>
{% endif %}
